    {
      "question": "The statements print 70,519 as 'Property taxes', but the General Fund schedule shows it is total taxes (property 58,808, motor vehicle 6,957, Public Power District 5% 4,754). Split as recorded, or keep one property tax line?",
      "amount": 70519,
      "recorded_as": "split into property tax 58,808, motor vehicle tax 6,957, Public Power District Sales Tax 4,754 (split_from), as in FY2023",
      "source_page": 4
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis city; choices follow FY2023. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p4, Total Governmental Funds); combined lines (Property taxes, Intergovernmental, Charges for services, Miscellaneous) split using the General, Street, CDBG, Cemetery and ARPA fund schedules, which add exactly. Business-type lines from the modified cash proprietary statement (p6, Total; ties to the Statement of Activities p2); accrual-basis proprietary statements (pp18-20) are supplementary and not used. Debt service 12,545 split into interest 1,779 and principal 10,766 from the cash flow statement (p7). Business-type receipts total computed; disbursements total from the Statement of Activities (268,767). Cash/investments: beginning from the 2021 Total column of p3; CDs recorded as investments; the fund balance roll-forward reconciles (cash alone moves with the CD balance). Detail: per-fund budget schedules (General, Street, Lottery, CDBG, Cemetery, ARPA; ARPA prints no totals line); utility funds only on the combined all-funds budget schedule (p9), one expenditure line per fund. Budget-only lines with no actual (Contracted services, Electricity, Supplies, Maintenance, Street repairs, Grant/Loan proceeds, CDBG interest and Housing rehab, General Fund transfers out) not recorded. Read pages 1-20 of 20"
}
